# This fixture's two sides are `base/` and `target/`, and those names are not
# cosmetic: `_resolve_side` treats the literal refs `base` and `target` as
# selecting that subdirectory as the state root, which is how c020-c023 compare
# the two sides.
#
# `target/` is also a build-output ignore default (Rust, Maven), so for *query*
# cases -- which index the fixture root rather than one side -- half this
# fixture was invisible. q034 asks "where is `process` in the target tree?" and
# could only ever be answered from `base/`, because `target/processor.py` was
# excluded from every index. Its recall was structurally 0 and always had been.
#
# Re-included here rather than by renaming the directory, which would break the
# ref grammar above, and rather than marking the cases unmeasured, which would
# make ADR-0024's honest "the adapter declined to run this" signal mean two
# things. `.codeatlasignore` is compiled with `overrides=True`, so this beats
# the builtin default; the default itself is untouched and still applies to
# every other repository.
#
# Change cases are unaffected: they select `base/` or `target/` as the state
# root, so this file sits above them and is never read for them.
!target/
